{
  "title": {
    "id": "title",
    "x": 400,
    "y": -2,
    "width": 800,
    "height": 60,
    "z": 1,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": "font-size: 60px;text-align:center",
    "text": "SORT: Parameters"
  },
  "overview": {
    "id": "overview",
    "x": 108,
    "y": 80,
    "width": 1400,
    "height": 150,
    "layer": -3,
    "z": 1,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": "font-size: 25px; ",
    "html": "Beyond <b>key</b> and <b>reverse</b>, SORT has parameters that pick what gets sorted and how values compare. <b>groupBy</b> stacks a fanned hand into one group per value of a property. An <b>order</b> array pins a custom sequence for one key. <b>locales</b> and <b>options</b> are handed to JavaScript's localeCompare, and <b>collection</b> with <b>rearrange</b> sorts a SELECTed collection without moving a thing. Every button below runs one of them. Click a button in edit mode to see the detail."
  },
  "button1": {
    "type": "button",
    "id": "button1",
    "x": 129,
    "y": 215,
    "height": 40,
    "text": "groupBy: 'suit'",
    "clickRoutine": [
      {
        "func": "SORT",
        "holder": "hand",
        "key": "rank",
        "groupBy": "suit"
      }
    ],
    "width": 160
  },
  "button2": {
    "type": "button",
    "id": "button2",
    "x": 537,
    "y": 215,
    "height": 40,
    "text": "groupBy: 'rank'",
    "clickRoutine": [
      {
        "func": "SORT",
        "holder": "hand",
        "key": "suit",
        "groupBy": "rank"
      }
    ],
    "width": 160
  },
  "button3": {
    "type": "button",
    "id": "button3",
    "x": 953,
    "y": 215,
    "height": 40,
    "text": "Suits in a fixed order",
    "clickRoutine": [
      {
        "func": "SORT",
        "holder": "hand",
        "key": [
          {
            "key": "suit",
            "order": [
              "H",
              "C",
              "D",
              "S"
            ]
          },
          "rank"
        ],
        "groupBy": "suit"
      }
    ],
    "width": 200
  },
  "dealButton": {
    "type": "button",
    "id": "dealButton",
    "x": 1359,
    "y": 215,
    "height": 40,
    "text": "Deal 12 cards",
    "clickRoutine": [
      {
        "func": "MOVE",
        "from": "deckHolder",
        "to": "hand",
        "count": 12,
        "face": 1
      }
    ],
    "width": 150
  },
  "text1": {
    "id": "text1",
    "x": 14,
    "y": 270,
    "width": 350,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": {
      "font-size": "22px"
    },
    "html": "<b>groupBy</b>: in a holder that fans groups (<i>layout: \"multiSpread\"</i>), SORT stacks one group per value of that property. <b>Key</b> sorts inside each group. This also works on collections (for example, one player's cards only)."
  },
  "text2": {
    "id": "text2",
    "x": 421,
    "y": 270,
    "width": 350,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": {
      "font-size": "22px"
    },
    "html": "<i>groupBy: \"rank\"</i> regroups the same cards by rank instead. Pairs and triples land in one fan. Then <i>key: \"suit\"</i> orders each of them."
  },
  "text3": {
    "id": "text3",
    "x": 836,
    "y": 270,
    "width": 350,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": {
      "font-size": "22px"
    },
    "html": "<b>order</b>: an array inside a key object fixes the sequence by hand: <i>{key: \"suit\", order: [\"H\", \"C\", \"D\", \"S\"]}</i> puts hearts first and spades last. Values missing from the list sort after it. Combined with <b>groupBy</b> the fans themselves line up in that order."
  },
  "text4": {
    "id": "text4",
    "x": 1234,
    "y": 270,
    "width": 350,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": {
      "font-size": "22px"
    },
    "html": "The deal lands in the hand as one single fan. Split it up with the buttons, drag cards between the fans, and start over any time: Recall &amp; Shuffle, then deal a fresh dozen."
  },
